  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "localId": "9462d3b25f9e"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "When a username is sent in the On-Behalf-Of header to Fedora, it will be used in WebAC authentication. We believe that it should also be used to update the ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ],
       "text": "fedora: createdBy",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ],
       "text": "fedora: lastModifiedBy",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " triples (the UpstreamAuth feature in Fedora 3.3+ did this too). This enables applications which implement their own authn/authz and are talking to Fedora via admin account to transparently act on behalf of the upstream user, which is important for audit purposes.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
