       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2e3b8d69747fdc1ece397990e2d18bf2?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRH-6.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2e3b8d69747fdc1ece397990e2d18bf2?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRH-6.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2e3b8d69747fdc1ece397990e2d18bf2?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRH-6.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Rastislav Hudak",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5ec7d5f8b12d2b0c2f92cdf8",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=70121%3Abc4e5839-97af-495c-9ccd-ae12309a105a\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"70121:bc4e5839-97af-495c-9ccd-ae12309a105a\" data-account-id=\"70121:bc4e5839-97af-495c-9ccd-ae12309a105a\" accountid=\"70121:bc4e5839-97af-495c-9ccd-ae12309a105a\" rel=\"noreferrer\">David Novák</a> Yes that’s fair. But if Fedora already accepts On-Behalf-Of and uses it in authorization, it would make sense to also emit a provenance triple for it. Leaving this to clients is duplication and creates inconsistency. Since using fedora:createdBy/fedora:lastModifiedBy would mask the actual account, using another triple would be fine for us too. <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" data-account-id=\"6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" accountid=\"6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Jared Whiklo</a> would that be an alternative?</p>",
